            <ArticleTitle>Congenital atresia of left main coronary artery: proposed mechanism for severe disabling angina in a patient with non-atherosclerotic single right coronary artery--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with progressive disabling angina was found to have a single right coronary artery with atresia of the left main coronary artery, and absence of any obstructive coronary disease. The patient required aortocoronary by-pass surgical reconstruction of a left main coronary artery to control her angina. Possible mechanisms for the development of her anginal pain are briefly discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
